  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 200 PM MDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nFriday starts off this long term period with the upper level ridge \nstaying put and the trough moving to the east, tilting toward the \nnortheast. A westerly flow comes to the 700mb height as the ridge \nbegins to weaken and push out of the area. 700mb winds increase with \nthe height gradient tightening. Surface winds are expected to be \nstronger and gusty. Carbon county can expect to see the strongest \nand gustiest winds. Temperatures at 700mb increase between 15 to 19C \nin the afternoon on Friday. Afternoon minimum humidity values are \nexpected to be between 15 to 20 percent for much of the CWA. This \nalong with gusty winds brings elevated fire weather conditions. \n\nAn upper level trough moves through the PNW through this long term \nperiod. Upper level flow increases as the weekend progresses, \nsupporting chances for showers and storms on Saturday and Sunday. \nSunday looks to be an active day with a trough starting to \nnegatively tilt over central Montana. A strong jet develops \nstretching from eastern Montana through Western Nebraska. Sunday \nafternoon will have strong forcing due to much of the region being \nin the right entrance region of the upper level jet. Some models \nshow good WAA at 700mb. This coupled with the strong upper level jet \nprimes the atmosphere for strong storms on Sunday. More to come as \nwe get closer to Sunday. Monday and Tuesday bring more chances for \nstorms and showers. Temperatures stay warm through Saturday then \ncool off starting on Sunday, bringing more seasonable temperatures \nas we head into September.",
